// @check
// @error operator '==' is not defined for i32 and string
// CONTRACT (must-error): the deferred binary-op capability check covers EQUALITY, not just
// arithmetic and comparison. `cmp`'s params are inference holes, so `a == b` cannot be decided
// in the body; the call site re-validates it under the substituted argument types and finds
// `i32 == string`, which `equality-type-mismatch.vl` already rejects in its annotated spelling.
//
// This is the cell where a miss is worse than a wrong answer: VL has no cross-type equality, so
// the emitter has no lowering for one, and an accepted `i32 == string` emits an i32 where the
// module declares a `(ref $type)` — the engine rejects the whole module at instantiation, which
// is a compile-clean program that cannot run at all.
function cmp(a, b) a == b

print(cmp(1, "x"))
